# SPDX-License-Identifier: AGPL-3.0-or-later
#
# GlintfxPkgConfigValidateInstalled.cmake.in - PKG-VALIDATE / PKG-NATIVE.
#
# Configured with configure_file(@ONLY) by
# glintfx_register_pkgconfig_validation() (cmake/GlintfxPkgConfigValidate.cmake)
# into <build>/GlintfxPkgConfigValidateInstalled.cmake, then
# include()-d from ONE install(CODE) line appended right after
# glintfx.pc's own install(FILES ...) (glintfx_install_pkgconfig(),
# cmake/GlintfxInstall.cmake). By the time this file runs, glintfx.pc,
# the public headers and the library artifact are already on disk, in
# whatever real layout THIS `cmake --install` invocation actually
# produced, on the machine actually running it - a packager we have
# never met, using a layout tests/tools/check_pkgconfig.sh (PKG-DIST)
# never enumerated (GODS_LAWS.md LEI ZERO: the base of consumers is
# public and unknown, so a validator that only runs in our CI leaves
# every layout outside it unchecked, silently).
#
# PKG-NATIVE (27/08/2026) - THE HAND-WRITTEN READER IS GONE. Decision
# of the lider (ESCOPO.md paragraph 7, "A exigencia minima da
# ferramenta de build SOBE, e o leitor caseiro morre"): the
# hand-written pkg-config text reader that used to live in this file
# (glintfx_pkgconfig_read_raw_variables(), glintfx_pkgconfig_resolve_variables(),
# glintfx_pkgconfig_substitute_text(), glintfx_pkgconfig_lookup_variable(),
# glintfx_pkgconfig_read_field() - all now deleted) was reopened by
# adversarial review FIVE times in two days, always the same family: a
# path fragment entering from one more source without being made
# absolute first (relative --prefix, relative DESTDIR, CWD-dependent
# resolution of a relative includedir/libdir/-I/-L value). GODS_LAWS.md
# L-42 ("uma falha revista mais de uma vez -> buscar na web"): CMake's
# OWN build-in pkg-config format parser, cmake_pkg_config(), added in
# CMake 3.31 (EXTRACT only) and completed with IMPORT/POPULATE in
# CMake 4.1 - "generates CMake variables and targets from pkg-config
# format package files natively, without needing to invoke or even
# require the presence of a pkg-config implementation" (CMake's own
# documentation, cmake_pkg_config.html) - now does every byte of
# tokenizing, comment-stripping, whitespace-around-"=" handling,
# Cflags:/Libs: field splitting and "-I"/"-L"/"-l" token extraction
# this file used to hand-roll. cmake_minimum_required(VERSION 4.1) in
# the root CMakeLists.txt is the reason this project's floor moved
# (see that file's own comment, and PACKAGING.md's "CMake version
# requirement" section, for which of the five platforms needed a CI
# install step to reach it - measured, not assumed: Fedora 44 ships
# 4.3.0, Arch and CachyOS ship 4.4.2, all comfortably above the floor
# with no CI step needed; Ubuntu 24.04's apt and the windows-latest
# GitHub Actions runner both ship BELOW 4.1 (3.28.3 and 3.31.6
# respectively, the second one measured against actions/runner-images'
# own Windows2025-Readme.md, not assumed from the Linux-only text of
# ESCOPO.md's own decision 7) and both get an explicit CMake-install
# step in .github/workflows/ci.yml).
#
# STRICTNESS STRICT (this file's every cmake_pkg_config() call) is the
# strictest mode the command offers - "closely mirrors the behavior of
# the original FDO pkg-config: variables and keywords must be unique
# [and] must be defined before they are used" (CMake's own
# documentation). Two MEASURED consequences worth naming plainly,
# because they are a real behavior change from the reader this file
# used to carry, not an accident:
#   - A glintfx.pc with the SAME variable defined twice, which the OLD
#     hand-written reader used to accept (last definition wins,
#     matching real pkgconf's own PERMISSIVE behavior) now FAILS
#     CLOSED under STRICT instead - measured live on this machine
#     (CMake 4.3.0): a two-line "libdir=" file that used to pass now
#     reports "cmake_pkg_config Resolution failed". This is a
#     narrowing, not a regression: glintfx's OWN generated glintfx.pc
#     never defines a variable twice (PACKAGING.md already documented
#     this as a property of glintfx.pc.in and cmake/GlintfxInstall.cmake,
#     unchanged by this fatia), so this only ever rejects a
#     hand-edited or packager-modified file that was already ambiguous
#     - and rejecting an ambiguous file is what "the strictest mode it
#     offers" is FOR.
#   - "${pcfiledir}" - pkg-config's own built-in for "the directory
#     this .pc file is actually in", which glintfx.pc.in's whole
#     relocatable-prefix design depends on ("prefix=${pcfiledir}/../..")
#     - is NOT a variable cmake_pkg_config() resolves on its own.
#     MEASURED, twice, two different ways (an absolute PC_FILE argument
#     and a PC_LIBDIR-searched package name): "${pcfiledir}" is silent-
#     empty under the default STRICTNESS PERMISSIVE, and a hard
#     "Resolution failed" under STRICT ("must be defined before used" -
#     pcfiledir is never assigned by a "key=value" line, because it is
#     supposed to be a BUILT-IN). Searched for a CMake issue tracker
#     entry naming this gap explicitly (L-42) and found none; the CMake
#     documentation for cmake_pkg_config() (fetched 27/08/2026) never
#     mentions "pcfiledir" at all, in either direction. Confirmed as a
#     genuine, present-day gap in this version of the native
#     mechanism, not a usage mistake on this file's part.
#
#     THE FIX, and it is the ONLY hand-written text operation this file
#     still performs: glintfx_pkgconfig_prepare_native_input() below
#     copies glintfx.pc's own text to a private SCRATCH file (never the
#     real installed glintfx.pc - a packager's install tree is never
#     written to by this validation) and replaces the literal token
#     "${pcfiledir}" with pc_file's own, already-absolute PARENT_PATH -
#     a value this file already computes today for exactly this
#     purpose, never predicted, never CWD-dependent. This is a single,
#     universally-quoted, exact-substring string(REPLACE ...) - not a
#     parser, not a tokenizer, not a variable-resolution engine: those
#     three things are exactly what cmake_pkg_config() now does, on the
#     SUBSTITUTED file, in the ONE call this file makes to it. Every
#     other pkg-config syntax question (comments, whitespace,
#     duplicate detection, "${var}" chains through prefix/exec_prefix/
#     libdir/includedir, Cflags:/Libs: tokenizing) is answered by CMake
#     itself from this point on.
#
# WHAT THIS DOES NOT TRY TO HANDLE, DECLARED (GODS_LAWS.md L-27,
# honest downgrade over silent overclaiming):
#   - Cross-compilation needs nothing special here: every check below
#     either reads the filesystem/calls cmake_pkg_config() (no binary
#     involved at all - see "Talking to the pkg-config BINARY itself"
#     below) or runs `pkg-config`/`pkgconf`, a HOST tool operating on
#     text (the one binary-conversation check) - neither ever executes
#     the target-arch library or an object file, so nothing here is
#     target-arch sensitive.
#   - Component-scoped installs (`cmake --install --component X`) need
#     nothing special either, and this is a property of THIS PROJECT
#     today, not a general claim: none of glintfx's install() rules
#     (library, headers, CMake package, glintfx.pc, and this
#     validation's own install(CODE)) declare a COMPONENT, so they all
#     share the implicit default component, and a `--component <name>`
#     install for any OTHER name installs NOTHING for glintfx at all -
#     this validation is skipped right along with it, for the same
#     reason, not by any special-casing here.
#   - What "Libs.private carries the right linker token for a static
#     build" MEANS (its content, and that it is genuinely load-bearing
#     for a real static link) is PKG-DIST's own, already-tested claim
#     (tests/tools/check_pkgconfig.sh's static scenario). This file
#     only proves every PATH glintfx.pc emits (via a plain,
#     non-`--static` `--cflags`/`--libs` query - the one every
#     consumer hits) resolves to something real.
#   - Windows library-artifact naming: RESOLVED (PKG-WIN-SCOPE,
#     revertido por ordem do lider, 27/08/2026). glintfx.pc is
#     installed on Windows the same as everywhere else, and the glob
#     below (glintfx_pkgconfig_library_glob_patterns()) matches
#     glintfx.lib too, alongside libglintfx.so*/libglintfx.a.
#   - Talking to the pkg-config BINARY itself, as opposed to reading
#     the filesystem/calling cmake_pkg_config(), is where this file
#     still draws its one platform-shaped line (unchanged by
#     PKG-NATIVE - this half never used the hand-written reader, and
#     is not what the lider's decision replaced). Every filesystem/
#     cmake_pkg_config()-only check runs UNCONDITIONALLY, before this
#     file ever tries to find or talk to a pkg-config binary, on every
#     platform, Windows included, with FATAL_ERROR veto power that
#     never downgrades. What DOES still talk to a real pkg-config
#     binary: confirming that a REAL pkg-config on THIS machine's PATH
#     also finds glintfx via `--exists` - a genuinely different claim
#     than "the content glintfx.pc describes is really on disk", and
#     the only one that can plausibly vary by which pkg-config a
#     packager happens to have. On GitHub Actions' windows-latest
#     runner, the only pkg-config on PATH is Strawberry Perl's
#     Pure-Perl `PkgConfig` reimplementation (`pkg-config.bat`), which
#     - MEASURED against a live fixture by
#     tools/ci/diagnose-win-pkgconfig.ps1 - resolves a bare
#     PKG_CONFIG_PATH value shaped like "C:/Users/.../pkgconfig" (no
#     explicit list separator) by falling back to POSIX-style splitting
#     on ':', which shreds the drive letter itself ("C:") into a bogus
#     one-letter search directory; the SAME value with an explicit
#     trailing ';' resolves correctly. That measured fix - append a
#     native list separator before talking to pkg-config on Windows -
#     is applied below, unchanged by PKG-NATIVE. If the conversation
#     with the binary still fails after that fix,
#     glintfx_validate_installed_pkgconfig() reports it as a WARNING on
#     Windows, not a FATAL_ERROR, and names ONLY that one conversation
#     as unverified: the filesystem/cmake_pkg_config() content check
#     above it already ran, on THIS same invocation, and already had
#     full veto power over whatever it found.
#   - DESTDIR is Unix-only BY THE BUILD TOOL'S OWN DOCUMENTATION, not
#     by anything this file assumes: "DESTDIR may not be used on
#     Windows because installation prefix usually contains a drive
#     letter like in C:/Program Files which cannot be prepended with
#     some other prefix" (CMake's own envvar/DESTDIR.html, fetched
#     27/08/2026). glintfx_pkgconfig_validate_resolve_staged_dir()
#     below still reads $ENV{DESTDIR} unconditionally (a real packager
#     could still set it on Windows and get a nonsensical path - CMake
#     itself does not refuse it), but no scenario this project tests
#     combines DESTDIR with a Windows install, because no supported
#     Windows packaging pipeline does either.
#
# Two escape hatches, both named GLINTFX_SKIP_PKGCONFIG_VALIDATION on
# purpose (one name, two mechanisms, same intent): the CACHE option in
# cmake/GlintfxOptions.cmake, read at CONFIGURE time by
# glintfx_register_pkgconfig_validation() BEFORE this file is even
# generated (skips it for good, for this build directory); and the
# ENVIRONMENT variable read at the top of
# glintfx_validate_installed_pkgconfig() below, at INSTALL time -
# because a packaging pipeline that configures ONCE and installs
# SEVERAL times against different DESTDIR/--component values (a real
# pattern: RPM's `%install` section can invoke `%cmake_install` more
# than once) should not have to reconfigure the whole tree just to
# skip this one check on one of those invocations.
#
# Each function below does one thing (GODS_LAWS.md L-17).

# Forces `value` (a CMake variable NAME, passed by reference the way
# every other in-place helper in this file does) absolute, anchored to
# `base_directory` - a REQUIRED, EXPLICIT argument, never CMake's own
# implicit default (CMAKE_CURRENT_SOURCE_DIR, silently applied whenever
# BASE_DIRECTORY is left out of a raw cmake_path(ABSOLUTE_PATH ...)
# call). Two call sites in
# glintfx_pkgconfig_validate_resolve_staged_dir() below share this one
# atom instead of each repeating the same three-line pattern - the
# earlier shape of this file (PKG-WIN-SCOPE round 6, before PKG-NATIVE)
# fixed CMAKE_INSTALL_PREFIX's own relative-path doubling this way and
# left $ENV{DESTDIR} unfixed, which is the SAME class of bug one call
# site later: a real `cmake --install` resolves a relative --prefix
# AND a relative DESTDIR against the invoking process's CWD, the exact
# rule CMAKE_CURRENT_SOURCE_DIR already answers correctly in script
# mode (confirmed against a real generated cmake_install.cmake on this
# machine).
function(glintfx_pkgconfig_force_absolute value_var base_directory)
    set(_glintfx_absolute_value "${${value_var}}")
    cmake_path(ABSOLUTE_PATH _glintfx_absolute_value BASE_DIRECTORY "${base_directory}" NORMALIZE)
    set(${value_var} "${_glintfx_absolute_value}" PARENT_SCOPE)
endfunction()

# Resolves the STAGED (DESTDIR-aware) pkgconfig/ directory this
# install actually wrote glintfx.pc into - never a predicted value,
# only the same inputs GNUInstallDirs' own install() rules already
# used to decide where to write it for real. Unrelated to PKG-NATIVE's
# own subject (this resolves WHERE the file is, never WHAT is inside
# it - see this file's own header for why the reader that answers the
# second question is gone and this function is not).
function(glintfx_pkgconfig_validate_resolve_staged_dir out_var)
    cmake_path(SET _glintfx_configured_libdir NORMALIZE "@GLINTFX_NORMALIZED_INSTALL_LIBDIR@")

    if(IS_ABSOLUTE "${_glintfx_configured_libdir}")
        # GNUInstallDirs allows CMAKE_INSTALL_LIBDIR to be absolute (a
        # packager staging into a fixed system location outside
        # CMAKE_INSTALL_PREFIX) - install() ignores CMAKE_INSTALL_PREFIX
        # entirely for an already-absolute DESTINATION, so this branch
        # must too (same rule glintfx_compute_pkgconfig_relocatable_prefix()
        # in cmake/GlintfxInstall.cmake already applies to glintfx.pc's
        # OWN prefix= content). CMAKE_INSTALL_PREFIX never enters this
        # branch at all.
        set(_glintfx_dir_no_destdir "${_glintfx_configured_libdir}/pkgconfig")
    else()
        # A relative --prefix must resolve the SAME way `cmake --install`
        # itself resolves it - against the invoking process's CWD, not
        # glintfx.pc's own eventual pcfiledir - which is exactly what
        # omitting an explicit pcfiledir-style base and using
        # CMAKE_CURRENT_SOURCE_DIR (the invoking CWD in script mode)
        # gives glintfx_pkgconfig_force_absolute() here.
        set(_glintfx_prefix "${CMAKE_INSTALL_PREFIX}")
        glintfx_pkgconfig_force_absolute(_glintfx_prefix "${CMAKE_CURRENT_SOURCE_DIR}")
        cmake_path(APPEND _glintfx_prefix "${_glintfx_configured_libdir}" "pkgconfig"
            OUTPUT_VARIABLE _glintfx_dir_no_destdir)
    endif()

    if(DEFINED ENV{DESTDIR} AND NOT "$ENV{DESTDIR}" STREQUAL "")
        # DESTDIR is Unix-only by the build tool's own documentation
        # (see this file's header) - a real packaging pipeline that
        # sets it is staging into a subdirectory of its own choosing,
        # which real `cmake --install` resolves against the SAME
        # invoking-CWD rule as a relative --prefix (measured:
        # "-- Installing: <cwd>/<destdir>/..." from a real relative-
        # DESTDIR install on this machine). Forced absolute first,
        # through the same atom as CMAKE_INSTALL_PREFIX above, before
        # being concatenated onto an already-absolute destination -
        # deliberately a PLAIN STRING PREFIX, never cmake_path(APPEND),
        # which treats an absolute right-hand side as "replace the
        # base", the opposite of what DESTDIR means (mirrors what
        # CMake's own file(INSTALL) does internally, for the same
        # reason PACKAGING.md documents: "DESTDIR prepends to EVERY
        # destination, relative or absolute, without changing any path
        # baked into the installed files' own content").
        set(_glintfx_destdir "$ENV{DESTDIR}")
        glintfx_pkgconfig_force_absolute(_glintfx_destdir "${CMAKE_CURRENT_SOURCE_DIR}")
        set(_glintfx_staged_dir "${_glintfx_destdir}${_glintfx_dir_no_destdir}")
        cmake_path(SET _glintfx_staged_dir NORMALIZE "${_glintfx_staged_dir}")
        set(${out_var} "${_glintfx_staged_dir}" PARENT_SCOPE)
    else()
        set(${out_var} "${_glintfx_dir_no_destdir}" PARENT_SCOPE)
    endif()
endfunction()

# Filesystem patterns that name glintfx's own compiled library
# artifact, one glob per platform-shaped naming convention it is known
# to produce (cmake/GlintfxLibrary.cmake's OUTPUT_NAME "glintfx" is the
# same string on every platform; only the prefix/suffix a linker
# actually writes to disk differ). A single source of truth, shared by
# both content-check call sites below (GODS_LAWS.md L-17).
function(glintfx_pkgconfig_library_glob_patterns out_var)
    set(${out_var}
        "libglintfx.so*"
        "libglintfx.a"
        # glintfx.lib: Windows/MSVC ARCHIVE artifact
        # (cmake/GlintfxInstall.cmake's install(TARGETS ... ARCHIVE
        # DESTINATION ...)) - the SAME extension names both a shared
        # build's import library and a static build's archive there,
        # so one pattern covers both.
        "glintfx.lib"
        PARENT_SCOPE
    )
endfunction()

# THE ONLY HAND-WRITTEN TEXT OPERATION LEFT IN THIS FILE (see this
# file's own header, "STRICTNESS STRICT", for why it exists at all):
# copies pc_file's own text to a private scratch file under
# @GLINTFX_VALIDATE_SCRATCH_DIR@ (a build-tree location, never the
# packager's own install tree) and replaces every literal
# "${pcfiledir}" token with pc_file's own, already-absolute
# PARENT_PATH - a single, exact-substring string(REPLACE ...), not a
# parser: no "${...}" is evaluated, no comment is stripped, no
# whitespace is trimmed. cmake_pkg_config(EXTRACT ...) below does all
# of that, natively, on the result.
#
# One scratch file per validation run is enough - this file's own
# install(CODE) registration runs this whole script exactly once per
# `cmake --install` invocation (glintfx_register_pkgconfig_validation(),
# cmake/GlintfxPkgConfigValidate.cmake) - so there is no concurrent-
# write hazard to guard against here.
function(glintfx_pkgconfig_prepare_native_input pc_file out_scratch_file)
    file(READ "${pc_file}" _glintfx_pc_text)
    cmake_path(GET pc_file PARENT_PATH _glintfx_pcfiledir)
    string(REPLACE "\${pcfiledir}" "${_glintfx_pcfiledir}" _glintfx_pc_text_substituted "${_glintfx_pc_text}")

    set(_glintfx_scratch_dir "@GLINTFX_VALIDATE_SCRATCH_DIR@")
    file(MAKE_DIRECTORY "${_glintfx_scratch_dir}")
    set(_glintfx_scratch_file "${_glintfx_scratch_dir}/glintfx.pc")
    file(WRITE "${_glintfx_scratch_file}" "${_glintfx_pc_text_substituted}")

    set(${out_scratch_file} "${_glintfx_scratch_file}" PARENT_SCOPE)
endfunction()

# Validates ONE "-I"/"-L"-token LIST (already extracted by
# cmake_pkg_config(EXTRACT ...) into CMAKE_PKG_CONFIG_INCLUDES or
# CMAKE_PKG_CONFIG_LIBDIRS - see glintfx_pkgconfig_validate_content_native()
# below) against real content on disk: every token strips its own
# "-I"/"-L" prefix and must resolve to a directory containing the
# expected content: a "glintfx/" subdirectory for headers, or one of
# glintfx_pkgconfig_library_glob_patterns() for the library artifact.
# flag_prefix is "-I" or "-L"; expected_content_kind is "headers" or
# "library" - the only two things any path glintfx.pc emits ever
# names, the same two shapes tests/tools/check_pkgconfig.sh's own
# assert_dir_contains_expected_content already checks in CI.
# GODS_LAWS.md L-40 floor: out_count is always set, even to zero - the
# CALLER decides whether zero is a failure, this function only counts
# and validates what it is given.
#
# ANCHORED TO pcfiledir, NEVER LEFT CWD-DEPENDENT - MEASURED, not
# assumed: a bare relative "-L"/"-I" token straight out of
# CMAKE_PKG_CONFIG_INCLUDES/LIBDIRS (no leading "/", the shape a
# tampered "libdir=some-relative-name" line - with no "${...}"
# reference at all - produces) is left EXACTLY as relative by
# cmake_pkg_config() itself; CMake's own IS_DIRECTORY on a relative
# path resolves it against CMAKE_CURRENT_SOURCE_DIR, which in script
# mode is the CALLER's CWD - reproduced live, twice, once from a
# directory holding a decoy "libglintfx.so*" under that same relative
# name (IS_DIRECTORY reported TRUE) and once from an unrelated empty
# directory (IS_DIRECTORY reported FALSE, same token, same file). This
# is the EXACT "biblioteca apagada, descritor com caminho relativo,
# comando disparado de dentro de uma pasta com uma biblioteca falsa"
# attack this whole validator exists to refuse - and it is a NEW
# finding, specific to routing token resolution through
# cmake_pkg_config() instead of the deleted hand-written reader (the
# old reader anchored to pcfiledir directly; the native command hands
# back a token that may still be bare-relative, and does not anchor it
# for us). Fixed the same way the old reader fixed it: every token is
# forced absolute against pc_file's OWN, already-absolute parent
# directory - never CMAKE_CURRENT_SOURCE_DIR, never anything a
# packager's invocation directory can influence - via
# glintfx_pkgconfig_force_absolute(), defined above.
function(glintfx_pkgconfig_validate_content_tokens pc_file tokens flag_prefix expected_content_kind out_count)
    cmake_path(GET pc_file PARENT_PATH _glintfx_tokens_pcfiledir)
    set(_glintfx_count 0)
    foreach(_glintfx_token IN LISTS tokens)
        if(NOT _glintfx_token MATCHES "^${flag_prefix}(.+)$")
            continue()
        endif()
        set(_glintfx_path "${CMAKE_MATCH_1}")
        glintfx_pkgconfig_force_absolute(_glintfx_path "${_glintfx_tokens_pcfiledir}")

        if(NOT IS_DIRECTORY "${_glintfx_path}")
            message(FATAL_ERROR
                "glintfx: glintfx.pc's own '${flag_prefix}' field emitted "
                "'${_glintfx_token}', which resolves to '${_glintfx_path}', "
                "which does not exist on disk (pc file: "
                "'${pc_file}'). Skip this check with "
                "GLINTFX_SKIP_PKGCONFIG_VALIDATION=1 in the environment "
                "of this `cmake --install` invocation, then verify the "
                "install by hand."
            )
        endif()

        if(expected_content_kind STREQUAL "headers")
            if(NOT IS_DIRECTORY "${_glintfx_path}/glintfx")
                message(FATAL_ERROR
                    "glintfx: glintfx.pc's own '${flag_prefix}' field "
                    "emitted '${_glintfx_token}', which resolves to "
                    "'${_glintfx_path}' - it exists, but has no "
                    "'glintfx/' subdirectory, so the installed public "
                    "headers are not there (pc file: '${pc_file}'). "
                    "Skip this check with "
                    "GLINTFX_SKIP_PKGCONFIG_VALIDATION=1 in the "
                    "environment of this `cmake --install` invocation, "
                    "then verify the install by hand."
                )
            endif()
        elseif(expected_content_kind STREQUAL "library")
            glintfx_pkgconfig_library_glob_patterns(_glintfx_lib_pattern_names)
            set(_glintfx_lib_glob_patterns "")
            foreach(_glintfx_lib_pattern_name IN LISTS _glintfx_lib_pattern_names)
                list(APPEND _glintfx_lib_glob_patterns "${_glintfx_path}/${_glintfx_lib_pattern_name}")
            endforeach()
            file(GLOB _glintfx_lib_matches ${_glintfx_lib_glob_patterns})
            if(_glintfx_lib_matches STREQUAL "")
                message(FATAL_ERROR
                    "glintfx: glintfx.pc's own '${flag_prefix}' field "
                    "emitted '${_glintfx_token}', which resolves to "
                    "'${_glintfx_path}' - it exists, but has none of "
                    "${_glintfx_lib_pattern_names}, so the installed "
                    "library artifact is not there (pc file: "
                    "'${pc_file}'). Skip this check with "
                    "GLINTFX_SKIP_PKGCONFIG_VALIDATION=1 in the "
                    "environment of this `cmake --install` invocation, "
                    "then verify the install by hand."
                )
            endif()
        else()
            message(FATAL_ERROR
                "glintfx: glintfx_pkgconfig_validate_content_tokens: "
                "unknown expected_content_kind '${expected_content_kind}' "
                "(internal error in glintfx's own install(CODE) "
                "validation - this is not something a packaging layout "
                "can trigger)."
            )
        endif()

        math(EXPR _glintfx_count "${_glintfx_count} + 1")
    endforeach()
    set(${out_count} "${_glintfx_count}" PARENT_SCOPE)
endfunction()

# Orchestrates the WHOLE content check (LAYER A) against ONE installed
# glintfx.pc, natively: prepares the pcfiledir-substituted scratch copy
# (glintfx_pkgconfig_prepare_native_input(), above - the one hand-
# written text operation this file still performs), hands it to
# cmake_pkg_config(EXTRACT ... STRICTNESS STRICT) - CMake's own native
# pkg-config format parser, no pkg-config binary involved (see this
# file's header, "Talking to the pkg-config BINARY itself") - and
# validates every "-I"/"-L" token it extracts against real content on
# disk. GODS_LAWS.md L-40 floor: a Cflags:/Libs: line with no "-I"/"-L"
# token at all makes cmake_pkg_config() return an EMPTY list, not an
# error (measured: CMAKE_PKG_CONFIG_INCLUDES/LIBDIRS both come back
# empty, with exit 0, against a real glintfx.pc with blank "Cflags:"/
# "Libs:" fields) - the explicit EQUAL 0 checks below are what turn
# that silent "nothing to report" into the FATAL_ERROR L-40 requires;
# cmake_pkg_config() itself does not do this for us. FATAL_ERROR on
# every platform, Windows included, unconditionally - this is the
# check that used to run only AFTER a pkg-config binary conversation
# had already succeeded (PKG-WIN-SCOPE's original finding, still true
# today, unrelated to PKG-NATIVE): glintfx_validate_installed_pkgconfig()
# below calls this BEFORE it ever tries to find or talk to a
# pkg-config binary, on purpose.
function(glintfx_pkgconfig_validate_content_on_disk pc_file)
    glintfx_pkgconfig_prepare_native_input("${pc_file}" _glintfx_native_input)

    cmake_pkg_config(EXTRACT "${_glintfx_native_input}" REQUIRED STRICTNESS STRICT)

    glintfx_pkgconfig_validate_content_tokens(
        "${pc_file}" "${CMAKE_PKG_CONFIG_INCLUDES}" "-I" headers _glintfx_include_flag_count
    )
    glintfx_pkgconfig_validate_content_tokens(
        "${pc_file}" "${CMAKE_PKG_CONFIG_LIBDIRS}" "-L" library _glintfx_library_flag_count
    )

    if(_glintfx_include_flag_count EQUAL 0)
        message(FATAL_ERROR
            "glintfx: glintfx.pc's own Cflags: field emitted ZERO -I "
            "flags (pc file: '${pc_file}') - an empty Cflags: line "
            "would make this validator scan nothing and still report "
            "success (GODS_LAWS.md L-40). Skip this check with "
            "GLINTFX_SKIP_PKGCONFIG_VALIDATION=1 in the environment of "
            "this `cmake --install` invocation, then verify the "
            "install by hand."
        )
    endif()
    if(_glintfx_library_flag_count EQUAL 0)
        message(FATAL_ERROR
            "glintfx: glintfx.pc's own Libs: field emitted ZERO -L "
            "flags (pc file: '${pc_file}') - an empty Libs: line would "
            "make this validator scan nothing and still report success "
            "(GODS_LAWS.md L-40). Skip this check with "
            "GLINTFX_SKIP_PKGCONFIG_VALIDATION=1 in the environment of "
            "this `cmake --install` invocation, then verify the "
            "install by hand."
        )
    endif()

    message(STATUS
        "glintfx: post-install pkg-config content check (CMake's own "
        "native pkg-config parser, cmake_pkg_config(EXTRACT ... "
        "STRICTNESS STRICT) - no pkg-config binary involved) - "
        "${_glintfx_include_flag_count} -I flag(s) and "
        "${_glintfx_library_flag_count} -L flag(s) all resolve to "
        "real, populated directories."
    )
endfunction()

function(glintfx_validate_installed_pkgconfig)
    if(DEFINED ENV{GLINTFX_SKIP_PKGCONFIG_VALIDATION}
       AND NOT "$ENV{GLINTFX_SKIP_PKGCONFIG_VALIDATION}" STREQUAL ""
       AND NOT "$ENV{GLINTFX_SKIP_PKGCONFIG_VALIDATION}" STREQUAL "0")
        message(STATUS
            "glintfx: post-install pkg-config validation skipped - "
            "GLINTFX_SKIP_PKGCONFIG_VALIDATION is set in the "
            "environment of this `cmake --install` invocation."
        )
        return()
    endif()

    glintfx_pkgconfig_validate_resolve_staged_dir(_glintfx_pkgconfig_dir)
    set(_glintfx_pc_file "${_glintfx_pkgconfig_dir}/glintfx.pc")

    if(NOT EXISTS "${_glintfx_pc_file}")
        message(FATAL_ERROR
            "glintfx: expected to find glintfx.pc at "
            "'${_glintfx_pc_file}' right after installing it, and it "
            "is not there. This usually means CMAKE_INSTALL_LIBDIR, "
            "CMAKE_INSTALL_PREFIX or DESTDIR combined in a way this "
            "validation step did not anticipate. Skip this check with "
            "GLINTFX_SKIP_PKGCONFIG_VALIDATION=1 in the environment of "
            "this `cmake --install` invocation (or reconfigure with "
            "-DGLINTFX_SKIP_PKGCONFIG_VALIDATION=ON to disable it "
            "permanently for this build), then verify the install by "
            "hand."
        )
    endif()

    # LAYER A, unconditional, on EVERY platform, BEFORE this file ever
    # tries to find or talk to a pkg-config binary: CMake's own native
    # pkg-config parser confirms includedir/libdir and every -I/-L
    # token resolve to real, populated content on disk
    # (glintfx_pkgconfig_validate_content_on_disk(), defined above).
    glintfx_pkgconfig_validate_content_on_disk("${_glintfx_pc_file}")

    find_program(GLINTFX_PKGCONFIG_VALIDATE_EXE NAMES pkg-config pkgconf NO_CACHE)
    if(NOT GLINTFX_PKGCONFIG_VALIDATE_EXE)
        message(WARNING
            "glintfx: pkg-config (and pkgconf) not found on PATH - "
            "skipping the pkg-config BINARY conversation "
            "('pkg-config --exists glintfx'). glintfx.pc was written "
            "to '${_glintfx_pc_file}', and its content already passed "
            "this file's own native content check (includedir, libdir, "
            "and every -I/-L token confirmed against real content on "
            "disk by CMake's own pkg-config parser); there is simply "
            "no pkg-config/pkgconf on PATH to additionally confirm a "
            "REAL pkg-config binary also resolves it. Install "
            "pkg-config (or pkgconf) to get that extra confirmation, "
            "or set GLINTFX_SKIP_PKGCONFIG_VALIDATION=1 to silence "
            "this warning intentionally."
        )
        return()
    endif()

    # Unchanged by PKG-NATIVE - this half never used the hand-written
    # reader, and is not what the lider's decision replaced. See this
    # file's own header, "Talking to the pkg-config BINARY itself".
    if(WIN32)
        cmake_path(CONVERT "${_glintfx_pkgconfig_dir}" TO_NATIVE_PATH_LIST _glintfx_pkgconfig_path_native)
        string(APPEND _glintfx_pkgconfig_path_native ";")
        set(ENV{PKG_CONFIG_PATH} "${_glintfx_pkgconfig_path_native}")
    else()
        set(ENV{PKG_CONFIG_PATH} "${_glintfx_pkgconfig_dir}")
    endif()

    execute_process(
        COMMAND "${GLINTFX_PKGCONFIG_VALIDATE_EXE}" --print-errors --exists glintfx
        RESULT_VARIABLE _glintfx_exists_result
        ERROR_VARIABLE _glintfx_exists_error
        OUTPUT_QUIET
    )
    if(NOT _glintfx_exists_result EQUAL 0)
        if(WIN32)
            # The LAYER A content check above has ALREADY run,
            # unconditionally, by the time this line can even be
            # reached, and it is what actually confirmed glintfx.pc,
            # the headers and the library artifact are genuinely on
            # disk with real content - not this `--exists` call, and
            # not any other check below it. What could NOT be
            # confirmed is whether THIS pkg-config binary, on THIS
            # machine, can also find and parse glintfx.pc via
            # PKG_CONFIG_PATH - a binary-specific quirk this file
            # cannot enumerate for every Windows pkg-config that could
            # exist (GODS_LAWS.md L-27: declared downgrade, not a
            # silent "ok").
            message(WARNING
                "glintfx: post-install pkg-config CONVERSATION could not "
                "be verified on this Windows machine - 'pkg-config "
                "--exists glintfx' failed against the file just "
                "installed at '${_glintfx_pc_file}' "
                "(PKG_CONFIG_PATH=$ENV{PKG_CONFIG_PATH}): "
                "${_glintfx_exists_error}. This file's OWN native "
                "content check already ran before this point (CMake's "
                "own pkg-config parser, no pkg-config binary involved) "
                "and already confirmed glintfx.pc, the headers and the "
                "library artifact are genuinely on disk with real "
                "content; only whether THIS machine's pkg-config "
                "binary additionally resolves them via PKG_CONFIG_PATH "
                "is unverified. Set GLINTFX_SKIP_PKGCONFIG_VALIDATION=1 "
                "to silence this warning intentionally, or verify by "
                "hand with the pkg-config on this machine."
            )
            return()
        endif()
        message(FATAL_ERROR
            "glintfx: 'pkg-config --exists glintfx' failed against "
            "the file just installed at '${_glintfx_pc_file}' "
            "(PKG_CONFIG_PATH=${_glintfx_pkgconfig_dir}): "
            "${_glintfx_exists_error}. Skip this check with "
            "GLINTFX_SKIP_PKGCONFIG_VALIDATION=1 in the environment of "
            "this `cmake --install` invocation, then verify the "
            "install by hand."
        )
    endif()

    message(STATUS
        "glintfx: post-install pkg-config validation passed - "
        "glintfx.pc at '${_glintfx_pc_file}' passed this file's own "
        "native content check, and a real pkg-config binary on this "
        "machine's PATH also finds it via PKG_CONFIG_PATH."
    )
endfunction()

glintfx_validate_installed_pkgconfig()
